# what links.yml is told not to check, each line a regex and each with
# the measurement that put it here.

# Stack Overflow answers a runner 403 whatever the request looks like --
# measured with curl carrying a current Chrome user agent and an
# Accept: text/html header, from a residential address rather than a
# datacenter one -- while the page it names is live in a browser. The
# block is the host's policy on automated requests, so a checker can
# only ever report it as rot, and reporting it once a week is what
# would teach a reader to stop reading this workflow's output.
^https://stackoverflow\.com/
